List a directory being deleted with the platform's path delimiter.

DoRecursiveDeleteFile lists the directory's entries with FileName + L"\\*".
On POSIX the backslash is not a path delimiter: the search looked in the
parent directory for a name "<dir>\*", found nothing, and so the directory
was not deleted (the temporary folders' cleanup failed for an empty one).
Built with IncludeTrailingBackslash, as the rest of core builds paths, the
delimiter is the platform's: on Windows the same backslash as before, so
upstream's behaviour is unchanged. Line counts are unchanged.

--- a/source/core/Common.cpp
+++ b/source/core/Common.cpp
@@ -2506,1 +2506,1 @@
-        Result = (FindFirstUnchecked(FileName + L"\\*", faAnyFile, SearchRec) == 0);
+        Result = (FindFirstUnchecked(IncludeTrailingBackslash(FileName) + L"*", faAnyFile, SearchRec) == 0);
